truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha28) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NVMe: emergency reconnect ignores reconnect_attempted.

    Alpha27 diagnostic proved every failed activate_volume ran the
    emergency block and skipped with:
      emergency reconnect SKIPPED (reconnect_attempted=1) —
      a prior mid-loop reconnect already fired

    Root cause: some earlier mid-loop reconnect (usually i==10
    stale-NGUID) fires ~1s into the retry loop, BEFORE TN has
    finished publishing the target namespace. That reconnect
    completes but the kernel view stays stale-for-a-different-
    reason: TN just hasn't sent AER for the new namespace yet.
    The loop continues, still cannot find target, exhausts, then
    the emergency block silently declines to reconnect a second
    time because reconnect_attempted was already 1. The
    single-reconnect cap was killing recovery.

    Fix: emergency block ignores reconnect_attempted. Cost is
    ~500ms extra NVMe drop on the shared subsystem, worst case
    twice per failing activate_volume. Benefit: recovery from the
    "reconnect fired too early" case. Trade-off favors recovery.

