truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha24) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NVMe: last-resort reconnect at i==125 that ignores the fuser gate.

    Alpha23's halfway reconnect (i==75) never fires in multi-node
    steady-state — there is always SOME other VM using SOME device
    on the shared subsystem, and the fuser check declares the whole
    subsystem too busy to reconnect. The failure keeps happening
    with 0 halfway-reconnects logged.

    Alpha24: add a second trigger at i==125 (~12.5s in, ~2.5s of
    budget left) that forces the reconnect regardless of the fuser
    check. Rationale: at this point the retry loop is going to fail
    anyway. A confirmed activate_volume failure is worse for the
    user than a few hundred milliseconds of NVMe I/O pause on other
    VMs — kernel NVMe controller-loss handling normally resumes
    cleanly on reconnect. Same "target UUID confirmed on TN" gate
    as i==75, so we still don't disrupt anything on a bad UUID.

    Log message distinguishes "i==75 halfway" from "i==125 last-resort"
    and notes when the fuser gate was overridden.

