 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 18:30:00 +0000

truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha16) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Prefork the broker worker pool (N=4). The single-threaded accept
    loop was serializing every client RPC through one upstream WS --
    measured on pve, 4 concurrent broker calls that could parallelize
    took 9.8 s wall (last call queued behind all others) vs the fastest
    call finishing in 0.14 s. Under 3-node cluster test load, this
    stacked on top of TN's own contention: extent.create (3-6 s) and
    targetextent.create (7-8 s) on ONE alloc, then serial-queued on the
    broker with pool.dataset.query from pvestatd and other workers'
    calls, pushed body time past the pveproxy 60 s ceiling with three
    nodes hitting the shared cluster_lock_storage.

    Parent creates the listen fd + workers, then supervises: each
    worker inherits the listen fd and runs the original accept loop
    with its own persistent %POOL WS (auth'd once at worker startup).
    Kernel serializes accept() across workers so no thundering-herd
    race. Workers install their own TERM handler to close their WS
    cleanly on shutdown without touching the parent's socket / pidfile.
    Parent handler signals all workers, waits briefly for them to
    exit, then unlinks the runtime files.

    N=4 keeps auth cost well under TN's 20 / 60 s / IP rate limit on
    auth.login_with_api_key (4 auths at broker startup + occasional
    reconnect churn) while giving 4-way parallelism per node.

 -- TrueNAS Proxmox Plugin Maintainers <noreply@github.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0000

