truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Cap alloc_image's deferred device-verify at ~2 s instead of the
    latent 480 s worst case. The deferred discovery already ran an
    8-attempt best-effort outer loop with 250 ms between attempts,
    but each iteration called _device_for_lun which itself blocks up
    to tn_device_ready_retries * 100 ms (default 600 = 60 s) waiting
    for the by-path symlink to appear. Nested that is 8 x 60 s = 480 s
    per alloc, which under 3-node concurrent load routinely burned
    the pveproxy 60 s window on VM_add-disk PUTs and left VM-config
    locks held past the test-framework 180 s ceiling (test class A
    cascades from cluster_test_run 2026-08-17). _device_for_lun now
    accepts an optional max_retries_override, and the deferred alloc
    path passes 1 so the inner call collapses to a single check --
    the outer 250 ms retry loop is the actual retry budget for this
    best-effort path, and activate_volume remains the authoritative
    60 s wait when the VM starts. Non-deferred callers (path,
    activate_volume, snapshot device activation) still get the full
    default timeout.

