truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.23~alpha8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix retry classifier false-positive that turned every benign
    "dataset already exists" collision into a 3x retry storm under
    cluster load (cluster_test_run 2026-08-17 3-node runs, VM 179).
    Two related changes:

    - _is_connection_error: dropped the /WebSocket.*closed/ alternative.
      middlewared's JSON-RPC error payload embeds Python object reprs
      like `RpcWebSocketApp object at 0x...` and later `EventLoop ...
      closed=False`; the wildcard between them matched the class name
      to the closed=False attribute even when the underlying error was
      a plain ZFS collision. The WS-specific broker patterns (WS read,
      WS write, WS len, WS payload) plus the generic timeout / reset /
      connection-refused alternatives already cover every real
      WS-close failure our broker or upstream emits.

    - _is_retryable_error: added an explicit early return-0 for
      /dataset already exists|EZFS_EXISTS|zfs_create.*failed/i, gated
      before the connection-error check so a false-positive there
      cannot resurface. alloc_image already has an auto-increment
      recovery for the "already exists" case; without this the
      retry_with_backoff loop was firing 3 times per collision before
      it ever reached that recovery, burning seconds on the shared
      cluster storage lock and pushing concurrent alloc requests past
      the pveproxy 60 s / test-framework 180 s ceilings.

