    call so the record gets recreated cleanly. Logs a syslog warning
    listing what it removed so operators can trace the historical
    corruption. ~alpha4 stopped fresh corruption; this heals existing
    corruption in-place so nodes upgraded from pre-alpha4 don't
    require manual /var/lib/iscsi/nodes cleanup.

