truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.20+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix installer health check auth false positive (#57 bug 1): inline-Perl
    $scfg builders used bare (unprefixed) keys, so tn_api_host/tn_api_key
    were never seen and health checks always reported "Authentication
    failed" regardless of key validity. Now use tn_-prefixed keys.
  * Fix installer hostname rejection (#57 bug 2): storage wizard only
    accepted a bare IP for the TrueNAS host. Added validate_host() to
    accept a hostname/FQDN too, matching what tn_api_host already accepts.
  * Fix unbound variable crash when editing existing storage (#57 bug 3):
    menu_edit_storage read bare-named fields (e.g. config_values[dataset])
    from a config_values array populated with tn_-prefixed keys, crashing
    under set -u. Loader now strips the tn_ prefix on load; a leftover
    config_values[tn_sparse] read was corrected to config_values[sparse].
  * Installer diagnostic calls always disabled TLS certificate verification
    (community PR #63 follow-up): once bug 1 above fixed the tn_-prefixed
    $scfg keys, the hardcoded tn_api_insecure => 1 became a real, always-on
    TLS bypass regardless of a storage's configured tn_api_insecure. A
    TN_API_INSECURE global (mirroring TN_API_PORT) now threads the
    configured value through menu_cleanup_orphans, detect_orphaned_resources,
    and run_health_check.

