truenas-proxmox-plugin (2.1.9+deb1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix snapshot rollback when intermediate snapshots exist. PVE's qm
    rollback contract is to revert the disk to the target snapshot and
    discard anything taken after. Plugin was passing recursive=0 to TN's
    pool.snapshot.rollback, so any intermediate snapshot on the same
    dataset blocked the rollback with TN 25.10's wrapped FileExistsError:
      "Cannot rollback: more recent snapshots exist. Use recursive=True
      to destroy them. [Errno 17] Failed to rollback ... File exists"
    Two changes: volume_snapshot_rollback now passes recursive=1; the
    _tn_snapshot_rollback fallback regex also matches the TN 25.10
    wording (was matching only the old libzfs message). Verified against
    TN 25.10 snapshot_rollback_impl.py: recursive=True triggers
    _destroy_newer_snapshots on the target dataset and does not touch
    clones (recursive_clones=False) or child datasets
    (recursive_rollback=False). Matches PVE::Storage::ZFSPoolPlugin
    semantics (which calls `zfs rollback -r`).

